eld is negative" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=-4x{y}^{2}.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/96/96c937cf10d45d8870a4a56e257d184dcf2e4caf11312c05df9f385f9c5ee7a8.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360825 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172041 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "75710e99-e13c-54ba-9401-486bfec15284" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Rectangular Regions Where a Slope Field Is Positive or Negative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b88eec4-4bca-5a0c-8880-b03758a9562c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438646} {:answer/id #uuid "d0b8d18f-d196-594c-8c33-0a3b063ff4fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0b8d18f-d196-594c-8c33-0a3b063ff4fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438647} :answer-field/id #uuid "a57f0197-ee41-5615-824b-b099007a4ea7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439352} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09a982b0-26c1-598f-bb2a-081c92298f83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438648} {:answer/id #uuid "c9e21d2c-a5eb-5d88-b6f1-1f1bb6ae21fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09a982b0-26c1-598f-bb2a-081c92298f83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438648} :answer-field/id #uuid "30a269a3-6717-5dbd-aa51-fbb9a794d6c2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439353} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ccb719f3-4ad9-549b-8f43-db9fde533258" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438650} {:answer/id #uuid "b9393b52-2c4f-58b9-9b1c-b3c269d74cac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9393b52-2c4f-58b9-9b1c-b3c269d74cac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438651} :answer-field/id #uuid "e284995b-eb87-5cca-a13d-12a99f42075a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a885d23a-7465-5389-b01f-26298ac26e61" :question/math-academy-id "q-97495" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(x+2)(y+2)$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>-2$ and $y>-2,$ the slope of the slope field is positive\n- **II.** At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<-2$ and $y>-2,$ the slope of the slope field is positive\n- **III.** At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<-2$ and $y<-2,$ the slope of the slope field is positive" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=(x+2)(y+2).$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=-2$ or $y=-2.$ This divides the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](images/7d/7d225d82eee3043380eda76506b28e81aee06d42a232348b91b0d5ceb04f3318.png)\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each of those four regions (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/bd/bd9eedd3b8d82415e8f3126236f2e3a3b4e326a7072057bbd21406da92a08139.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. If $x>-2$ and $y>-2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement II is false. If $x<-2$ and $y>-2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $x<-2$ and $y<-2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362211 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172041 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "75710e99-e13c-54ba-9401-486bfec15284" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Rectangular Regions Where a Slope Field Is Positive or Negative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4842db83-277f-5ac6-9756-7d71ed57a360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438652} {:answer/id #uuid "aff73e0e-7657-51b7-a7f5-1be162f86243" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4842db83-277f-5ac6-9756-7d71ed57a360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438652} :answer-field/id #uuid "3021006b-6d7f-5efe-b7a1-726f767d922d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439355} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a32b2ab2-8963-54b9-9a32-d18a9a92c5fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438654} {:answer/id #uuid "9b16c32e-6930-5573-ab6e-d3adf9fffe07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a32b2ab2-8963-54b9-9a32-d18a9a92c5fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438654} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9933f56-9026-5d7c-b64d-f7f6c2a23d9e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439356} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6c52061-cde6-58fd-9539-45c706276407" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438656} {:answer/id #uuid "fcf6408d-db98-52dd-9aa1-9d5f8b43eba0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcf6408d-db98-52dd-9aa1-9d5f8b43eba0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438657} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab818855-7afa-5726-ad99-5b0158d162ae" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439357}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3ca0f65d-7276-53ff-adf8-200ee3f85dcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-97534" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(x-1)(y-1)^{2}$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<1$ and $y<1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive\n- **II.** At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>1$ and $y<1,$ the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **III.** At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>1$ and $y>1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=(x-1)(y-1)^{2}.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=1$ or $y=1.$ This divides the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](images/07/075264fa042adc64e160a83f03a2b125dd5a9b0927fc3ed318778c0004689ec4.png)\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each of those four regions (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/57/5716d59a745fc148b504a4db523286d7c7209fe793fcf369a90d220125f7e9fb.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. If $x<1$ and $y<1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement II is false. If $x>1$ and $y<1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $x>1$ and $y>1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363108 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115299 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4b2e2b5-5692-5b4a-804f-7518ab214d08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437872} {:answer/id #uuid "3acb46da-0035-5f87-8672-6682f18cf559" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3acb46da-0035-5f87-8672-6682f18cf559" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437873} :answer-field/id #uuid "477f40a4-66af-5870-95c1-78ba941c5598" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438965} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c7886ec-2b7c-5184-ba5d-a9cfd3f447ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437874} {:answer/id #uuid "1b86766c-211b-5526-8849-1753bc7e2812" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c7886ec-2b7c-5184-ba5d-a9cfd3f447ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437874} :answer-field/id #uuid "76f4b7f4-de99-5ebc-a3fb-5f5fcbe4139b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438966} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d52184b-23ff-5d3d-be0f-8e48b9e54a9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437876} {:answer/id #uuid "545708f8-29e7-5393-a590-6497da645a2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d52184b-23ff-5d3d-be0f-8e48b9e54a9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437876} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b08613c-08bd-5a65-b4c6-d5cae5341709" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438967}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e8de2435-5f56-5017-bf79-0b535c719854" :question/math-academy-id "q-131718" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y+z=2 \\\\  & -2x+7y+2z=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system has no solution\n- **III.** The system is consistent independent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we can find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364365 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115299 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e2d5a83-8718-5bdf-8eb3-db892e2ab5e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438532} {:answer/id #uuid "8eaaea36-3739-5e8a-a1ed-efc15f9bc00b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e2d5a83-8718-5bdf-8eb3-db892e2ab5e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438532} :answer-field/id #uuid "8efd7542-c77b-5d4d-8f60-5468e0925423" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439295} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "763f0363-fe65-5380-acc8-6965de771643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438534} {:answer/id #uuid "be014b12-0b58-51d7-a7a3-d343e4554293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be014b12-0b58-51d7-a7a3-d343e4554293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438535} :answer-field/id #uuid "1338d41d-dfae-54bb-ada6-b58b1d8cc303" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439296} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f48fb77e-36ef-5915-aaab-7df2660d984a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438536} {:answer/id #uuid "84b40478-f69c-539e-aac5-dd183a05b951" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f48fb77e-36ef-5915-aaab-7df2660d984a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438536} :answer-field/id #uuid "7051a40c-c2de-5375-95a6-8801b39f67c5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439297}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "35b0295d-1e16-59cc-a201-696e791e0b7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74643" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x+2y=8 \\\\  & x+y=-2 \\\\  & x+\\frac{1}{2}y=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system has no solution\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+y=-2 \\\\ -y=14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $y=-14.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(-14)=-2\\,⟹\\,x=12.\n$$\n\n \nSo,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent.   \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366794 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c502c08e-cbb1-5442-bcb9-424b6777ac3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438664} {:answer/id #uuid "003139e8-881a-52b3-9ea9-221baca3d942" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c502c08e-cbb1-5442-bcb9-424b6777ac3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438664} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee174a06-895c-5583-812c-7c4468fa2511" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439361} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4493f073-130a-5643-b440-425f3034460d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438666} {:answer/id #uuid "0508c95e-9b72-5cb3-8464-ae610809503a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0508c95e-9b72-5cb3-8464-ae610809503a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438667} :answer-field/id #uuid "495bc1a5-e85e-5043-b4d4-3fe8b15554ed" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439362} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1502369-e88d-503e-90f4-0f6ab218c61c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438668} {:answer/id #uuid "516ece6f-6106-541c-abfc-8c583469231d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "516ece6f-6106-541c-abfc-8c583469231d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438669} :answer-field/id #uuid "e222facc-8617-59fb-b0f3-b2ffe6c181c7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439363}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2e3acb77-06f5-5592-8e02-3140d23a412e" :question/math-academy-id "q-9835" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $D$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $det(D)=1$\n- **II.** $D$ is a singular matrix\n- **III.** $det(D)=0$\n\n \n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(28-30)-2(7-5)+3(6-4) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-2-4+6 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(D)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements II and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369359 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133895 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f4f726e-d985-5915-a4d0-30cfa6f4b89b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ae6522b-d021-5d59-8cd6-f5304bdd55ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437758} {:answer/id #uuid "a8414dbe-30d0-5384-b8c5-62cc6232e458" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8414dbe-30d0-5384-b8c5-62cc6232e458" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437759} :answer-field/id #uuid "748fe4bc-f5a7-5f6e-a198-2ec4af1a9fb6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438908} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5fcddd5-827b-5326-b25a-877e35a9d273" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437760} {:answer/id #uuid "1f174d76-4611-5f5a-bb29-5066e184e17e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5fcddd5-827b-5326-b25a-877e35a9d273" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437760} :answer-field/id #uuid "93da9704-e1a5-5081-8553-7cd992df06d2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438909} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cffa29f7-20b1-5b11-99da-52f6143261ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437762} {:answer/id #uuid "c4926ca4-8616-57f1-a942-8235f95a7902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4926ca4-8616-57f1-a942-8235f95a7902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437763} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3c21734-8e5a-535d-ada3-66000108f100" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438910}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf5aefc1-27f1-5c4b-be31-6e2e9699a7da" :question/math-academy-id "q-126560" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the functions $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $P(x,y)={e}^{x+y}-\\frac{y}{2}$ and $Q(x,y)={e}^{x+y}+\\frac{x}{2}$\n- **II.** $P(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$ and $Q(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$\n- **III.** $P(x,y)=x$ and $Q(x,y)=x$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Pair I gives the required area.  In this case,\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={e}^{x+y}-\\frac{1}{2}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}={e}^{x+y}+\\frac{1}{2},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\n- Pair II does *not* give the required area.  Notice that \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Pair III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369366 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133895 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f4f726e-d985-5915-a4d0-30cfa6f4b89b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95f3c085-feb8-513f-add4-66aa98bd17ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437764} {:answer/id #uuid "5fe0d2ca-9939-5556-96db-9df34ee271ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fe0d2ca-9939-5556-96db-9df34ee271ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437765} :answer-field/id #uuid "18de6163-4953-583e-b212-b0337c772ec5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438911} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dc332b0-9c6c-52fb-9960-0a34a7b12892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437766} {:answer/id #uuid "218378a4-fbcd-5e98-8eff-a70c74b13433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4dc332b0-9c6c-52fb-9960-0a34a7b12892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437766} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d6dd72a-3e01-555e-a264-373480cb3397" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438912} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8116a580-f40c-5f87-8318-cb566921d6e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437768} {:answer/id #uuid "ebb283d0-c938-5e90-8f21-2d9015525c2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ebb283d0-c938-5e90-8f21-2d9015525c2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437769} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1cf9841-fb2d-5f21-9260-8a5cc7b8a700" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438913}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5decc408-adb2-55a3-accb-8195735690a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-126571" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the vector field $F(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $F(x,y)=⟨0,\\,x⟩$\n- **II.** $F(x,y)=⟨{e}^{y},\\,y⟩$\n- **III.** $F(x,y)=⟨-\\frac{y}{5}+\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,\\,\\frac{4x}{5}⟩$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if $F(x,y)=⟨P(x,y),\\,Q(x,y)⟩,$ where\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field I give the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\n- Pair II does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={e}^{y}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=0,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-{e}^{y}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Pair III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{5}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{4}{5},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369373 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133895 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f4f726e-d985-5915-a4d0-30cfa6f4b89b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5314efe-6d3d-5874-a4e8-e3bb02359b6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437782} {:answer/id #uuid "de7792c1-6264-5b26-a11b-f266fd2ffbf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5314efe-6d3d-5874-a4e8-e3bb02359b6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437782} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d9aea2b-8ded-5e68-bdc8-80f01907fab2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438920} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f3e2c30-0387-56e6-9017-184fe08df055" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437784} {:answer/id #uuid "cca9abd2-28b1-50b1-a0d7-213e565a3526" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f3e2c30-0387-56e6-9017-184fe08df055" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437784} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cf91cf4-1adf-55a1-bef6-7fd579465082" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438921} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e066b5f-ee40-571e-9d64-c19fe307ffad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437786} {:answer/id #uuid "5cbbfdda-889f-50b7-8d61-3c68b8acb082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cbbfdda-889f-50b7-8d61-3c68b8acb082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437787} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dea6355-4414-5031-bdce-266f0e70af29" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438922}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a19e15dc-6544-52f9-9d54-2c5e5b2885d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-126577" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the vector field $F(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $F(x,y)=⟨y,\\,y⟩$\n- **II.** $F(x,y)=⟨\\frac{y}{7},\\,\\frac{6x}{7}⟩$\n- **III.** $F(x,y)=⟨{e}^{x}-{e}^{-y},\\,x{e}^{-y}+x⟩$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if $F(x,y)=⟨P(x,y),\\,Q(x,y)⟩,$ where\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field I does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=0,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-1\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II does *not* give the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{1}{7}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{6}{7},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{5}{7}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III gives the required area.  Notice that \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={e}^{-y}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}={e}^{-y}+1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380657 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172085 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "019e5a17-1aab-565b-8881-447c86a9a7ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Two-Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "162499c9-d211-5946-8b2e-c019541c3034" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437606} {:answer/id #uuid "96e0faf2-fb61-5450-8ad0-ff90febe7fb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96e0faf2-fb61-5450-8ad0-ff90febe7fb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437607} :answer-field/id #uuid "428e492b-b338-505d-b794-6840361998af" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438832} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4078c42f-287d-5b03-8583-af065de039c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437608} {:answer/id #uuid "b2eb56cf-3f62-5c54-b952-b89ebe56b894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4078c42f-287d-5b03-8583-af065de039c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437608} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc0a8721-d4c0-531c-850b-a28514d4f48c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438833} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24149d6d-29cf-587b-9c73-d17502c56d1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437610} {:answer/id #uuid "642982e1-2a9a-5105-be2e-a1a9730e6358" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24149d6d-29cf-587b-9c73-d17502c56d1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437610} :answer-field/id #uuid "571b08b4-5fa1-5191-8779-09ec9667116b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438834}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1de1af2b-64e8-50cf-80c9-f414743fe7ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-122641" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $G(x,y)={x}^{2}\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j$\n- **II.** $H(t)=\\sqrt{t}\\,i+t{e}^{t}\\,j$\n- **III.** $K(x,y,z)=2x\\,i+y\\,j-3z\\,k$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $G(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$ to a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $H(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$  It assigns points in $R$ (not ${R}^{2}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $K(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380664 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172085 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "019e5a17-1aab-565b-8881-447c86a9a7ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Two-Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d1447082-f4e8-5788-a80e-d8c2f8b82522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437630} {:answer/id #uuid "747beaa6-cbb1-5ab8-b6f0-aac6db2ca380" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1447082-f4e8-5788-a80e-d8c2f8b82522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437630} :answer-field/id #uuid "89920c46-71c7-5175-8718-e990046088f6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438844} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5963b314-2add-567a-b457-6f81885a3dad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437632} {:answer/id #uuid "0a97ce34-6fad-5a23-a913-7a8c54c9939c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a97ce34-6fad-5a23-a913-7a8c54c9939c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437633} :answer-field/id #uuid "121c69dd-36e1-570a-bd6d-c832cafb4cd4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438845} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2852e063-18c2-5c27-805a-899fefe85cd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437634} {:answer/id #uuid "2d47eb09-37b1-5b48-8d81-6237d57c3ab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2852e063-18c2-5c27-805a-899fefe85cd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437634} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6caeebf-8412-599a-8bb3-625ed3e2bddb" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "502cb71c-02d6-5e14-a31b-2cee28a0a5ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-122656" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $M(x,y)=⟨y-{x}^{2},3x+{y}^{2},\\frac{1}{x+y}⟩$\n- **II.** $N(x,y)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1,1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x⟩$\n- **III.** $P(t)=⟨{t}^{3},\\sqrt{1-t}\\,⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $M(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It assigns points in  ${R}^{2}$ to vectors in ${R}^{3}$ (not in ${R}^{2}$).\n\n- The function $N(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$ to a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $P(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It assigns points in  $R$ \n(not ${R}^{2}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380678 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172085 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "019e5a17-1aab-565b-8881-447c86a9a7ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Two-Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "acbf2816-9f71-5351-b1d8-a801bf30542d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437636} {:answer/id #uuid "308d0f3d-2e87-5cc6-b65f-2f83e5267801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "308d0f3d-2e87-5cc6-b65f-2f83e5267801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437637} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbe68175-15ca-5f31-9cf5-5f03083fe4fb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438847} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0725d6f3-2622-5e9f-9c94-bfc7b72d7402" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437638} {:answer/id #uuid "81503c2a-ae1a-5a4d-882d-f15bf57c0190" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81503c2a-ae1a-5a4d-882d-f15bf57c0190" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437639} :answer-field/id #uuid "920a7af7-aee4-545a-b604-ad8eca5e6e88" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438848} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ceb42624-bc8c-5336-8d28-af87d45d5914" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437640} {:answer/id #uuid "fc8e9ded-65e6-530c-8fb7-a0624c962138" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ceb42624-bc8c-5336-8d28-af87d45d5914" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437640} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a744e92-3f60-596f-918f-2e9f6b8fc76b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438849}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5b352a16-fe6f-5946-bac9-7b334007947a" :question/math-academy-id "q-122675" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $C(x,y)=⟨\\frac{1}{x+y},{x}^{2}{e}^{y}⟩$\n- **II.** $D(x,y)=⟨{y}^{3}-3,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y)⟩$\n- **III.** $E(x,y)=⟨x+1,y+2,x-y⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $C(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x+y\\ne 0}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $D(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$ to a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $E(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{2}$ to vectors in ${R}^{3}$ (not ${R}^{2}$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}]}
